Prepared against karpathy/minGPT @ 37baab7 (master). NOT SUBMITTED UPSTREAM —
this campaign does not open external PRs or issues. Kept here as evidence that
issues.md I-1 is a one-line defect with a one-line fix.

`mingpt/utils.py` imports numpy at module scope, so `import mingpt` fails on a
clean install that followed the README (`pip install -e .`) with only the
declared dependency present. Historically masked because torch used to depend
on numpy; modern torch wheels do not.

--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ setup(name='minGPT',
       description='A PyTorch re-implementation of GPT',
       license='MIT',
       install_requires=[
             'torch',
+            'numpy',
       ],
 )

Reproduction of the failure:

    $ python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install torch
    $ .venv/bin/python -c "import mingpt.utils"
    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'numpy'
